Important Notes
==========================================

1. PLEASE BE PATIENT after reboot!
   - The web interface may take up to 5 minutes to start on first boot
   - Services need time to initialize after installation
   - Wait at least 2-3 minutes before checking service status

2. For group changes to take effect:
   - Log out and log back in to your SSH session, OR
   - Run: newgrp systemd-journal

3. If you cannot access the web UI:
   - Check that the web service is running: sudo systemctl status ledmatrix-web
   - Verify firewall allows port 5000: sudo ufw status (if using UFW)
   - Check network connectivity: ping -c 3 8.8.8.8
   - If WiFi is not connected, connect to LEDMatrix-Setup AP network

4. SSH Access:
   - SSH must be configured during initial Pi setup (via Raspberry Pi Imager or raspi-config)
   - This installation script does not configure SSH credentials

5. Useful Commands:
   - Check service status: sudo systemctl status ledmatrix.service
   - View logs: journalctl -u ledmatrix-web.service -f
   - Start/stop display: sudo systemctl start/stop ledmatrix.service

6. Configuration Files:
